Recursion is a programming technique in which a function calls itself.  The function is called a recursive function.  The recursive function calls itself until it reaches a base case, at which point it returns a result.  The base case is a condition that the function can evaluate to a result without calling itself again.  The recursive function is called a recursive algorithm.
